# Baseline security headers for every page and file.
# - X-Frame-Options / frame-ancestors: other sites cannot embed these pages in
#   a frame (clickjacking). The site itself may.
# - X-Content-Type-Options: browsers must not guess a file's type.
# - Referrer-Policy: other sites only learn the domain a visitor came from,
#   not the full page URL.
# - Permissions-Policy: the site never uses camera, microphone, location, etc.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()

/*.pdf
  Content-Disposition: inline

# Cross-posting assets (figures and covers) can be fetched by other sites,
# e.g. the dev.to editor, so cross-posts can attach them directly.
/blog-figures/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
